        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> It is [`L` by default](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6714e738555b1cfbef646a23af29aa113f91f4fe/doc/mini-files.txt#L157) and can be configured in `config.mappings.go_in_plus`.\r\n\r\nOh sorry. It was actually not that hard to understand, my bad, but maybe comments would help. \r\n\r\n```lua\r\nmappings = {\r\n\tclose = \"q\", -- close filetree\r\n\tgo_in = \"l\",\r\n\tgo_in_plus = \"<CR>\", -- open file & close filetree\r\n\tgo_out = \"h\",\r\n\tgo_out_plus = \"<BS>\",\r\n\tmark_goto = \"'\", -- go to bookmark\r\n\tmark_set = \"m\", -- set bookmark\r\n\treset = \"<BS>\", -- go back to $CWD\r\n\treveal_cwd = \"Y\",\r\n\tshow_help = \"g?\",\r\n\tsynchronize = \"<C-w>\", -- save changes\r\n\ttrim_left = \"<Left>\", -- ??\r\n\ttrim_right = \"<Right>\", -- ??\r\n},\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
